# Distribution / packaging
# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored 'build/' matches
# at any depth, which silently swallowed docs/features/build/README.md: the
# article existed locally, the tests passed locally, and CI failed because the
# file had never been committed.
/build/

# PyInstaller
#  Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#  before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
# PyInstaller emits *.manifest beside its build output, which is why this is
# ignored. A hand-written manifest that SHIPS is a source file, though: the one
# below declares per-monitor v2 DPI awareness, and losing it to this rule would
# produce a packaged build that Windows bitmap-stretches on any scaled display
# -- with nothing failing, because a missing manifest is not an error.
!installer/amulet.manifest

