# ──── end Desktop Material: Build artifacts ────  (dm-template:build-artifacts)

# ──── Repository-specific rules. Keep these LAST. ────
# A shared template was synced into this file and silently undid three rules
# that were each written after a real failure. Git resolves the LAST matching
# pattern, so these live at the end of the file on purpose: a template block
# appended above them can no longer take them back out.
#
# Nothing broke when it happened, which is the point. Every file below was
# already tracked, and Git never stops tracking a file because a rule started
# matching it -- so the whole tree stayed green while the next new file in any
# of these three places would have been invisible.

# An unanchored 'build/' matches at any depth and swallows this article. The
# file existed locally, the tests passed locally, and CI failed on a file that
# had never been committed.
!docs/features/build/
!docs/features/build/**

# PyInstaller emits *.manifest beside its build output. This one is a source
# file that SHIPS: it declares per-monitor v2 DPI awareness, and without it a
# packaged build is bitmap-stretched by Windows on any scaled display -- with
# nothing failing, because a missing manifest is not an error.
!installer/amulet.manifest

# *.spec from the same template would hide the PyInstaller spec that every
# packaged build is produced from.
!installer/Amulet.spec
